  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run `vite build` or open the scene in a browser, so I haven't seen it render. The shadow framing and fog density are the parts most likely to need adjusting.\n\n- **Instancing:** There is a ground plane plus three instanced nodes, so the whole forest is three draw calls. The nodes are 8,000 cylinder trunks, 8,000 cone canopies and 2,000 squashed-sphere rocks.\n- **Placement:** A seeded linear congruential generator places everything in a disc of radius 58, so the forest is identical on every load.\n- **Colour:** Canopies and rocks get per-instance colours from `colors`. Their base material is white so the instance colour isn't applied twice.\n- **Light and fog:** One directional light with `shadow: true`, plus a hemisphere light and a neutral environment for fill. Fog is `effects.fog` with `mode: \"exp\"` and density 0.0035, in the same colour as the background. I left the shadow settings at their defaults, as in the docs recipe.\n- **Camera:** `camera.orbit` at [0, 52, 92] looking at [0, 2, 0], with `autoRotate: 0.08` rad/s. That camera distance should keep the whole forest in view.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set from the first `onFrame` callback. I didn't confirm that callback fires after the first frame is drawn.\n\n",
